1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,656
THIS SERIES IS A WORK OF FICTION
CREATED FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:03,616
ANY SIMILARITY OR RESEMBLANCE
TO ACTUAL PERSONS, LIVING OR DEAD

3
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:05,656
OR TO REAL ORGANIZATIONS, INSTITUTIONS OR
RELIGIOUS GROUPS IS ENTIRELY COINCIDENTAL

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,080
The Family Closest to God's Hand.

5
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:09,320
I'll deny it if...

6
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:12,720
If you don't talk, no one will ever know.

7
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,720
Bitch!

8
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,920
Slap me. And I'll release this video.

9
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,176
NALIN: HOW ARE YOU?
NALIN: I'M WORRIED ABOUT YOU

10
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,600
Don't fall in love with him.

11
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,720
Get your revenge.

12
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:23,640
Whose is this?

13
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:25,080
STEVEJOB123 SENT A PICTURE

14
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,936
What's the big deal
over one tube of lipstick?

15
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:28,920
She sent me this photo just to gloat.

16
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,040
You know Chris is seeing someone else,
don't you?

17
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,000
I brought a friend over for dinner.

18
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,920
Hello. My name is Nalin.

19
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,600
Oh, Nalin!

20
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,080
Welcome. Please, come in.

21
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:49,120
This way.

22
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:58,240
Chris?

23
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:01,440
Chris?

24
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:05,240
Chris!

25
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:07,720
Are you okay?

26
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,120
Uh...

27
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:14,120
I'll go make a call to the hospital.

28
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:15,840
Something urgent came up.

29
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:35,240
Wow, this place is huge.
It feels so warm and cozy.

30
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:38,720
Oh, there's even a zebra!

31
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:43,080
Your house is lovely.

32
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:45,120
Thank you, dear.

33
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,400
Well, I'll go find
something for you to eat.

34
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,600
You chat with your friend, okay?

35
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:54,240
Come on, Tul. Come help me in the kitchen.

36
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,720
You never do that.

37
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:59,440
Right. You're right.

38
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:01,760
Well, then, I'll stay and chat with you.

39
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:07,880
Tuang, how did you and Nalin meet?

40
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:12,760
You seem a little older than my son,
don't you?

41
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,600
We met in Strikers World, Mom.

42
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:17,240
We got on the same team.

43
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,680
That's right.

44
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:22,920
Interesting.

45
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,440
I never knew girls played...

46
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:26,800
shooting games.

47
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:29,440
Mom, tons of girls play.

48
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,800
She's really good at strategy.

49
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:33,280
And she's a rusher too.

50
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:49,080
UNBLOCK
NALIN

51
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:52,960
WHY ARE YOU HERE?!

52
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,560
CHRIS P: WHY ARE YOU HERE?!

53
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:55,880
Sorry.

54
00:02:55,960 --> 00:03:00,720
CHRIS P: WHY ARE YOU HERE?!

55
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:06,520
CHRIS P: JUST LEAVE, PLEASE

56
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:09,520
You should check it. It might be important.

57
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,240
It's okay.

58
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:18,200
Oh, right...

59
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,560
Nalin is also a member of our church.

60
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:22,760
Is she?

61
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:25,120
How come I've never seen you before?

62
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,960
Do you have a group yet?

63
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,080
Not really, ma'am.

64
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,960
I was baptized recently.

65
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:39,000
Do you think you could
recommend one for me?

66
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:41,960
Well, you've come to the right place.

67
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:44,200
Why don't we go talk in my studio?

68
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:46,440
I'm working on a painting right now.

69
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,000
We can talk while I paint.

70
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:49,400
Come on. Let's go.

71
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,440
Why do you seem so eager
to talk to Nalin, Mother?

72
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,880
Why not just let the kids hang out?

73
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,480
- What's wrong with that?
- Mom, Grandma...

74
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:59,520
Can you two not fight for one day?

75
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:02,920
We're not fighting, sweetheart.

76
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,840
Our family loves each other.

77
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:07,680
I guess I'll go check on the food then.

78
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,800
Make yourself at home, Nalin.

79
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,160
Um... May I use the bathroom?

80
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:20,320
Of course.

81
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:30,400
Hey.

82
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,960
Are you really close with Nalin?

83
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:35,480
Yeah. We're pretty close.

84
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,600
We talk a lot while we play.

85
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:41,520
CHRIS P: WHY ARE YOU HERE?!
CHRIS P: JUST LEAVE, PLEASE

86
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,440
NALIN: I JUST WANTED TO TALK TO YOU

87
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:46,920
So you two got close
without ever seeing each other?

88
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:50,080
Since we didn't know
what each other looked like,

89
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:53,280
I felt comfortable opening up to her.

90
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:56,680
Like what?

91
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,240
Well...

92
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:02,880
things we can't tell people who know us.

93
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:04,880
Like...

94
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:06,640
our England plan.

95
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:22,920
I'll be right back.

96
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:24,720
Okay.

97
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:37,760
Who really are you?

98
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:45,040
Didn't my mother-in-law pay you enough?

99
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:47,760
Are you here to intimidate me?

100
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:52,960
Pay me?

101
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:59,880
Tuang said you're the only person
he told about our trip to England.

102
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:04,520
TUANGCA: I'M MOVING ABROAD, BRO
STEVEJOB123: REALLY? WHEN?

103
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,760
TUANGCA: NEXT WEDNESDAY NIGHT

104
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:07,040
STEVEJOB123: WHERE?

105
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,120
TUANGCA: BACK TO ENGLAND

106
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:13,360
Then my mother-in-law had someone stop us
at the airport.

107
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:15,760
Hello, Mr. Wichai.

108
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,200
- Please excuse me.
- Wait.

109
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,800
You forgot your lipstick.

110
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:30,840
May I have it...

111
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,440
Sure.

112
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,360
But which one?

113
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:38,240
The one you deliberately left here...

114
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:42,360
or the one you forgot in Chris's car?

115
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:46,800
The first one is mine.

116
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:50,560
You're a renowned lawyer.

117
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:54,160
Why are you so quick
to assume they're both mine?

118
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:58,640
Just because they look the same?

119
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,480
Look at the way they're worn.

120
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:07,280
The tips are worn down
at exactly the same angle.

121
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:08,960
You're not fooling me.

122
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:28,960
Oops.

123
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:30,760
You figured it out already.

124
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:35,280
I was hoping
to make you fight with Chris again.

125
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,320
Get out.

126
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:39,400
Not yet.

127
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:43,280
I haven't even had a
meal at God's house yet.

128
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,360
You...

129
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,520
Go ahead. Scream.

130
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:48,680
Come on. Throw a fit.

131
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:51,960
Then Tuang will find out
his father is cheating.

132
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,640
Do you want to slap me?

133
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:56,800
Come on.

134
00:08:57,440 --> 00:09:00,080
Let's ruin Chris's
image in front of his son.

135
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:01,640
Shall we?

136
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:03,160
But if you won't slap me...

137
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,120
I'll take these back.

138
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:09,040
See you at the dinner table, Ms. Tul.

139
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:13,160
Enjoy your meal.

140
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,640
Consider it my treat
before you go to court.

141
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:20,840
And thank you so much...

142
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,200
for the confession.

143
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,760
Aren't you eating, Chris?

144
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:47,000
They're all your favorites.

145
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,400
Dad, have you met Nalin at church?

146
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:57,000
I... I think I have.

147
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:00,360
I've met a lot of people at church.

148
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:04,960
Your father's a minister, honey.
Of course he knows everyone.

149
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,440
So...

150
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:09,880
you've heard my dad preach, Nalin?

151
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:12,440
Is he good? You can be honest.

152
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:17,520
Well, you're asking me
to criticize a renowned minister.

153
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:18,760
I wouldn't dare.

154
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:22,720
But I can tell you this,
I came to Pornhova Church...

155
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:24,920
because of Chris.

156
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:29,720
Really?

157
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:30,920
Yeah.

158
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,720
Aw, Dad. You're so cool!

159
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:38,240
Luca, eat your food. Enough talking.

160
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,360
Are you seeing anyone, Nalin?

161
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:44,200
You should pray at our church.

162
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,960
God has brought many couples together.

163
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,840
Many even got married there.

164
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:51,960
Right, Mother?

165
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:55,520
Oh, yes. Yes.

166
00:10:56,440 --> 00:11:00,200
The Lord always brings
good people together.

167
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:03,480
But He also keeps bad people away...

168
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:07,120
from those who sincerely have faith.

169
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:10,720
What's your type, Nalin?

170
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,960
Maybe I can introduce you to someone.

171
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:18,640
I like warm and caring men.

172
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:21,720
I grew up without much
love from my parents,

173
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:25,360
so I prefer older, more mature men.

174
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:28,760
Someone like Chris?

175
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:36,560
The daddy type, like my dad?

176
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:37,880
That might be hard to find.

177
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:44,760
I'm almost jealous of you, Ms. Tul.

178
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,240
The grilled scallops are good, you know?

179
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:49,640
If you're jealous of someone else's love,

180
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:51,400
you should be mindful.

181
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:57,040
Don't give in to your jealousy
and fall for someone who's already taken.

182
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,840
Mom...

183
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:03,560
She was just teasing you.

184
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:07,240
I know. Nalin wouldn't do that.

185
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:09,600
Right?

186
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:10,960
Yes.

187
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:13,800
You see, this balsamic...

188
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:16,120
if you let it age, it tastes divine.

189
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:19,560
Do you remember
when you put this ring on my finger, Chris?

190
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,240
You made a promise before God...

191
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:26,720
to love me and have only me
for the rest of your life.

192
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,840
And you've always shown me

193
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:31,440
how much you love me.

194
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:37,520
Oh? Are you finished already, Nalin?

195
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:40,480
Yes.

196
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:42,880
Care for some dessert?

197
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,520
I'm not quite done yet.

198
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:47,480
No, thank you.

199
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:50,920
I think I should be going.

200
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,960
You have such a warm and loving family.

201
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:09,840
Chris.

202
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,200
Chris!

203
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:14,320
Are you going to confess to Tul?

204
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:15,760
Are you crazy?

205
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:18,360
If she finds out, our
family will fall apart.

206
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:20,120
You think she doesn't already know?

207
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,960
- Did you hear what she said to Nalin?
- I did.

208
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:25,400
But there's no evidence.
She can't do anything.

209
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:28,000
Chris,

210
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:29,920
what if your wife files for divorce?

211
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:33,920
Then I'll have to face the truth.

212
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,520
No.

213
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,240
Absolutely not.

214
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:40,800
It'll affect your chances
of becoming Church Council president.

215
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:43,200
You can't get sued for divorce.
Absolutely not!

216
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:45,280
- I don't even want the position, Mom.
- You have to.

217
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,480
Act normal.

218
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:53,000
Don't confess anything.

219
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:24,640
Tul.

220
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:43,840
I...

221
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,480
If you're not ready...

222
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,600
you don't have to say it.

223
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:58,320
I've been having an affair.

224
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:03,600
Are you confessing because you want to,

225
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:07,320
or because you have no choice?

226
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:13,160
Who is she?

227
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,200
Answer me.

228
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:32,280
Tul... I made a mistake.

229
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,240
Let it end with me.

230
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:37,360
No.

231
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,120
It's Nalin, isn't it?

232
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:54,960
Well...

233
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:56,360
I...

234
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:58,400
I feel so guilty.

235
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:00,920
I've been fighting these feelings.

236
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:07,880
I know now that I was wrong.

237
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:11,000
I'm sorry, Tul. Can you forgive me?

238
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:14,400
If that woman had never
set foot in this house...

239
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:18,120
would you have confessed to me?

240
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:22,320
How long were you planning
to keep me in the dark?

241
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:24,320
You saw what she did.

242
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:27,280
That woman dragged our son into this!

243
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:36,160
Tell me what you want me to do.

244
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:38,240
I'll do anything.

245
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,040
I want a divorce.

246
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:06,080
If Chris were as awful
as our client's husband,

247
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:07,400
I'd support your decision.

248
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,800
But come on. He admitted
his mistake himself.

249
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:13,360
Even the court considers intent.

250
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:15,720
It's all up to your heart.

251
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:21,080
Chris destroyed our family.

252
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:25,000
So you're using divorce to punish him?

253
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:27,760
Who are you really punishing,

254
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,120
Chris, yourself, or Tuang?

255
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:35,240
Divorce should be a judgment.

256
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:38,440
Why don't you talk things out first?

257
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:40,520
Give him a suspended sentence.

258
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:34,400
Tuang?

259
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:37,200
It's okay, honey.
You just fell while playing.

260
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:39,760
Come on. Can you stand up?

261
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:40,680
Tul...

262
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:43,360
See? You did it. You're perfectly fine.

263
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:45,640
We should make sure he's okay.

264
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,560
Let me look at your hands, Tuang.

265
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:50,400
Move them. Try making fists.

266
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:52,320
Not hurt, right?

267
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:54,760
What about your knees?

268
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:57,760
On a scale of one to ten,

269
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:58,920
how much do they hurt?

270
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,200
- Two.
- Two?

271
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:04,520
Okay. Now try kicking your leg.

272
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,280
I think we should get him checked out.

273
